  READING: the KiDS tail at 44-310 kpc books (mean) ~16.0 M_b of non-settled mass per isolated halo:
  ~40-60x the settled supply at 0.31 Mpc, >> accreted-debris capacity. Neither rescue the record named
  closes: debris under-fills by ~an order, an edgeless supply over-closes the universe by ~2 orders.
  The data's absolute fit is poor for BOTH edge and no-edge (chi2 281/84 on 28 dof, CFG801) — the real
  outer profile is neither. Open fork (named discriminators):
  (i) two-halo/neighbor contamination survives the isolated cut (test: GAMA isolated sample, same statistic);
  (ii) the supply rule is NOT per-halo 5.364 (test: excess mass profile vs R^-1; debris shows a steeper fall);
  (iii) M_b bin means systematically low (Upsilon) (test: rerun with no-edge profile at +0.1 dex, CFG801 residual).
